* Device card for fecap_nls: TiN/MoOx/La:HZO 9 nm/Nb2O5/TiN capacitor of Mukherjee et al.,
* IEDM 2023 (doi:10.1109/IEDM45741.2023.10413879).  Generated by examples/tail_fit_study.py.
* Fitted: the reversible branches to the C-V of Fig. 5a, and the activation-field scales b+ / b-
* to the two switching-current peaks of the 50 us P-V loop.  Kinetics (tau0, alpha, beta) and the
* Dagum shape are the Alessandri 2019 values of the generic card (not fitted to this device).
* Not reproduced: the read endurance of Fig. 7 at -0.3 / -0.5 V.  With this card the first reads
* switch far too much; the data need the stored state to be 0.41-0.44 V harder to switch than in the loop
* (a stabilizing imprint; docs/research/tail-fit.md).  That shift is not part of this card.
* Instance parameters: area = 4.8e-09 m^2 (60 x 80 um^2), s0 = +1 or -1.
.model fecap_mukherjee2023 fecap_nls
+ tfe=9e-09
* ^ [m] ferroelectric thickness. Source: La:HZO thickness of the stack (data/literature/mukherjee2023_iedm_cv.csv)
+ ps=0.165
* ^ [C/m^2] saturation polarization. Source: remanent polarization used for this device in examples/literature_comparison.py (P-V loop, digitized, approx.)
+ emp=9.86281e+07
* ^ [V/m] Dagum scale of the activation field (+ direction). Source: FITTED: b+ scaled so that the + branch peak of the 50 us loop is at +1.35 V (switching current, examples/tail_fit_study.py)
+ emn=9.86281e+07
* ^ [V/m] Dagum scale of the activation field (- direction). Source: FITTED: b- scaled so that the - branch peak of the 50 us loop is at -0.54 V (same procedure)
+ ap=8.68421
* ^ [1] Dagum shape (core width), + direction. Source: Dagum refit of [Alessandri2019] (the generic card's distribution, not fitted to this device)
+ an=8.68421
* ^ [1] Dagum shape (core width), - direction. Source: Dagum refit of [Alessandri2019] (not fitted to this device)
+ pt=1.13582
* ^ [1] Dagum shape; low-field tail G ~ (E/b)^(a p). Source: Dagum refit of [Alessandri2019] (not fitted to this device); tail exponent a*p = 9.9
+ alpha=4.10978
* ^ [1] Merz-type exponent. Source: Dagum refit of [Alessandri2019] (not fitted to this device)
+ vimp=0.405
* ^ [V] built-in (imprint) voltage; loop centre. Source: centre of the loop's switching-current peaks +1.35 V and -0.54 V (digitized, approx.; examples/literature_comparison.py)
+ c_d=0.025279
* ^ [F/m^2] (1) linear dielectric capacitance (eps_r about 23 at 10 nm). Source: FITTED: Lorentzian branch fit to the C-V of Fig. 5a [Mukherjee2023IEDM] (7 points, 4 parameters)
+ dcap=0.0176356
* ^ [F/m^2] (2) peak height of each reversible branch. Source: FITTED: same C-V fit
+ vw=2.01198
* ^ [V] half width of each branch. Source: FITTED: same C-V fit
+ vs=1.62472
* ^ [V] distance of each branch peak from V_i. Source: FITTED: same C-V fit
+ vi=0.783
* ^ [V] crossing voltage of the two branches. Source: crossing point E_CROSS = 0.87 MV/cm of Fig. 5a (digitized)
